IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-carers-hours`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 1, regulations 89 to 92: the claimants who fall within
-- section 19 of the Act (subject to no work-related requirements), including by their earnings, and those who fall within
-- section 20 (work-focused interview requirement only).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- Each limb of regulation 89(1) and of regulation 91(2) is a rule of its own, with its own record of facts; the rule for the whole
-- paragraph takes the limbs' results. The text says "falls within section N of the Act" and nothing about the order of the sections,
-- which is the Act's: this module does not decide which group a claimant who meets two sets of conditions is in.
-- A fact decided by another regulation (regulation 3, 14 or 62, or Part 6) is a stated input, as the comment on it says.

§ `Work-related groups`

-- src:1389 | Work-related groups

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 89 — Claimants subject to no work-related requirements`

-- Limb (a): the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit (State Pension Credit Act 2002, not among the inputs).
-- out of range: the qualifying age for state pension credit (not among the inputs): whether the claimant has reached it is a stated input
-- src:1390 | 89 Claimants subject to no work-related requirements
-- src:1391 | (1) A claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimants subject to no work-related requirements) if—.
-- src:1392 | (a) the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit;
@ref reg 89(1)(a) (src:1390-1392)
GIVEN `the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(a) — the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` MEANS
    `the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`

-- Limb (b): the claimant has caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled persons for at least 35 hours a week but does not
-- meet the conditions for a carer's allowance, or have entitlement to carer support payment, and the Secretary of State is satisfied that
-- it would be unreasonable to require work search and work availability requirements. Paragraph (2): "severely disabled" has the meaning
-- in section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (not among the inputs): whether a person is severely disabled is a stated fact.
-- "does not meet ..., or have ..." is read as neither (fork F-89-1).
-- out of range: section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act and the law on carer's allowance and carer support payment (not among the inputs): whether the claimant meets or has them is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1393 | (b) the claimant has caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled persons for at least 35 hours a week but does not meet the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance , or have entitlement to carer support payment, and the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement and a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act;
@ref reg 89(1)(b) (src:1393)
-- src:1403 | (2) In paragraph (1)(b) “severely disabled” has the meaning in section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
@ref reg 89(2) (src:1403)
DECLARE `Caring for a severely disabled person` HAS
    `the claimant has caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled persons for at least 35 hours a week`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant meets the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has entitlement to carer support payment`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement and a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- out of range: section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act and the law on carer's allowance and carer support payment (not among the inputs): whether the claimant meets or has them is a stated input
@ref reg 89(1)(b) (src:1393)
GIVEN caring IS A `Caring for a severely disabled person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(b) — the claimant cares for a severely disabled person` caring MEANS
    (caring's `the claimant has caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled persons for at least 35 hours a week`)
    AND (NOT (caring's `the claimant meets the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance`))
    AND (NOT (caring's `the claimant has entitlement to carer support payment`))
    AND (caring's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement and a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act`)

-- Limb (c): the claimant is pregnant and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks
-- or less since the date of her confinement. The 11 weeks are counted back from the first day of the expected week, and the 15 weeks forward
-- from the date of confinement (fork F-89-2). "Confinement" is defined in regulation 2 and decided in regulation 8 (uc1): its date is a stated input.
-- src:1394 | (c) the claimant is pregnant and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement;
@ref reg 89(1)(c) (src:1394)
DECLARE `Pregnancy or confinement` HAS
    `the claimant is pregnant`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day of her expected week of confinement`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the claimant was pregnant`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of her confinement`                                        IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref reg 89(1)(c) (src:1394)
GIVEN pregnancy IS A `Pregnancy or confinement`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(c) — the claimant is pregnant or recently confined` pregnancy `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `11 weeks or less before the expected week of confinement`
    OR `15 weeks or less since the date of confinement`
    WHERE
        `11 weeks or less before the expected week of confinement` MEANS
            (pregnancy's `the claimant is pregnant`)
            AND (CONSIDER pregnancy's `first day of her expected week of confinement`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST expected THEN (Day expected MINUS Day `the date as at which it is asked`) AT MOST 77)
        `15 weeks or less since the date of confinement` MEANS
            (pregnancy's `the claimant was pregnant`)
            AND (CONSIDER pregnancy's `date of her confinement`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST confinement THEN
                     ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day confinement) AT LEAST 0)
                     AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day confinement) AT MOST 105))

-- Paragraph (3): "adopter" means a person who has been matched with a child for adoption and who is, or is intended to be, the responsible
-- carer for the child, but excluding a person who is a foster parent or close relative of the child; a person is matched with a child for
-- adoption when an adoption agency decides that the person would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child.
-- src:1404 | (3) In paragraph (1)(d)—
-- src:1405 | (a) “adopter” means a person who has been matched with a child for adoption and who is, or is intended to be, the responsible carer for the child, but excluding a person who is a foster parent or close relative of the child; and
-- src:1406 | (b) a person is matched with a child for adoption when it is decided by an adoption agency that the person would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child.
@ref reg 89(3) (src:1404-1406)
DECLARE `Adopter facts` HAS
    `an adoption agency has decided that the person would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is, or is intended to be, the responsible carer for the child`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's placement of the child as a foster parent`                                             IS A MAYBE `Placement of a child with a person`
    `the person's relation to the child`                                                                 IS A `Possible close relative`

@ref reg 89(3) (src:1404-1406)
GIVEN adopter IS AN `Adopter facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(3) — adopter` adopter MEANS
    (adopter's `an adoption agency has decided that the person would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child`)
    AND (adopter's `the person is, or is intended to be, the responsible carer for the child`)
    AND (NOT `a foster parent of the child`)
    AND (NOT (`reg 2 — close relative` (adopter's `the person's relation to the child`)))
    WHERE
        `a foster parent of the child` MEANS
            CONSIDER adopter's `the person's placement of the child as a foster parent`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST placement THEN `reg 2 — foster parent` placement

-- Limb (d): the claimant is an adopter and it is 12 months or less since (i) the date the child was placed with the claimant, or (ii) if the
-- claimant requested that the 12 months run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed, that date.
-- src:1395 | (d) the claimant is an adopter and it is 12 months or less since—
-- src:1396 | (i) the date that the child was placed with the claimant, or
-- src:1397 | (ii) if the claimant requested that the 12 months should run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed, that date;
@ref reg 89(1)(d) (src:1395-1397)
DECLARE `Adoption placement` HAS
    `date on which the child was placed with the claimant`                                                                                                IS A DATE
    `the claimant requested that the 12 months should run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date from which the claimant requested that the 12 months should run`                                                                            IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref reg 89(1)(d) (src:1395-1397)
GIVEN adopter IS AN `Adopter facts`
      placement IS AN `Adoption placement`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(d) — the claimant is an adopter within 12 months of the placement` adopter placement `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    (`reg 89(3) — adopter` adopter)
    AND (`12 months or less since the placement` OR `12 months or less since the requested date`)
    WHERE
        `12 months or less since the placement` MEANS
            `within 12 months of` (placement's `date on which the child was placed with the claimant`)
        `12 months or less since the requested date` MEANS
            (placement's `the claimant requested that the 12 months should run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed`)
            AND (CONSIDER placement's `the date from which the claimant requested that the 12 months should run`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST requested THEN `within 12 months of` requested)
        `within 12 months of` start MEANS
            ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day start) AT LEAST 0)
            AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` start (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))) AT MOST 0)

-- Paragraph (4): for the purposes of limb (e)(ii), a claimant is not to be treated as having student income where that income is a
-- postgraduate loan and the course in respect of which the loan is paid is not a full-time course. "Postgraduate loan" has the meaning
-- in regulation 68(7) (Part 6, uc2): whether the income is one is a stated input.
-- out of range: regulations 68 to 71 (piece uc2): whether the claimant has student income, or is treated as having it, is a stated input
-- src:1407 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e)(ii), a claimant is not to be treated as having student income where—
-- src:1408 | (a) that income is a postgraduate ... loan; and
-- src:1409 | (b) the course in respect of which that loan is paid is not a full-time course.
-- src:1410 | (5) In paragraph (4), “postgraduate ... loan” has the meaning given in regulation 68(7).
@ref reg 89(4) and (5) (src:1407-1410)
GIVEN `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that income is a postgraduate loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course in respect of which that loan is paid is a full-time course` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(4) — the claimant is treated as having student income` `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award` `that income is a postgraduate loan` `the course in respect of which that loan is paid is a full-time course` MEANS
    `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award`
    AND (NOT (`that income is a postgraduate loan` AND (NOT `the course in respect of which that loan is paid is a full-time course`)))

-- Limb (da): a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b) (uc1) who has student income in relation to the
-- course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award.
-- out of range: regulation 3(2)(b) (piece uc1): whether it applies is a stated input
-- out of range: regulations 68 to 71 (piece uc2): whether the claimant has student income, or is treated as having it, is a stated input
-- src:1398 | (da) the claimant is a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b) and has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award;
@ref reg 89(1)(da) (src:1398)
GIVEN `the claimant is a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(da) — a member of a couple with student income` `the claimant is a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b)` `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award` MEANS
    `the claimant is a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b)`
    AND `the claimant has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award`

-- Limb (e): the claimant does not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act (not receiving education) by virtue of regulation 14
-- (uc1) and (i) is a person referred to in paragraph (a) of that regulation, or (ii) has student income taken into account (paragraph (4)).
-- out of range: regulation 14 (piece uc1): whether it applies is a stated input
-- out of range: section 4(1)(d) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the claimant must meet the condition is a stated input
-- out of range: regulations 68 to 71 (piece uc2): whether the claimant has student income, or is treated as having it, is a stated input
-- src:1399 | (e) the claimant does not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act (not receiving education) by virtue of regulation 14 and—
-- src:1400 | (i) is a person referred to in paragraph (a) of that regulation (under 21, in non-advanced education and without parental support), or
-- src:1401 | (ii) has student income in relation to the course they are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of the award; or
@ref reg 89(1)(e) (src:1399-1401)
GIVEN `the claimant does not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act by virtue of regulation 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is treated as having student income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(e) — the claimant need not meet the condition of not receiving education` `the claimant does not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act by virtue of regulation 14` `the claimant is a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14` `the claimant is treated as having student income` MEANS
    `the claimant does not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act by virtue of regulation 14`
    AND (`the claimant is a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14` OR `the claimant is treated as having student income`)

-- Limb (f): the claimant is the responsible foster parent of a child under the age of 1.
-- src:1402 | (f) the claimant is the responsible foster parent of a child under the age of 1.
@ref reg 89(1)(f) (src:1402)
GIVEN foster IS A `Foster parents of a child`
      `the child is under the age of 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1)(f) — the responsible foster parent of a child under 1` foster `the child is under the age of 1` MEANS
    (`reg 85 — responsible foster parent` foster)
    AND `the child is under the age of 1`

-- Paragraph (1): a claimant falls within section 19 of the Act if any of the limbs applies.
@ref reg 89(1) (src:1390-1402)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      da IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 89(1) — the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` a b c d da e f MEANS
    `any limb applies`
    WHERE
        `any limb applies` MEANS any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb) (LIST a, b, c, d, da, e, f)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 90 — Claimants subject to no work-related requirements - the earnings thresholds`

-- The monthly amount that a person would be paid for a number of hours a week at an hourly rate, "converted to a monthly amount by
-- multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12", with any fraction of a pound disregarded (regulation 6(1A), which names regulation 90).
-- The same conversion is made in regulations 41(3), 99(6), 109 and 119; only regulations 90 and 99(6) disregard the fraction.
-- src:1416 | converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
@ref reg 90(2) (src:1416)
GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
      `hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` hours `hourly rate` MEANS
    `core — an amount with any fraction of a pound disregarded` ((hours TIMES `hourly rate` TIMES 52) DIVIDED BY 12)

@ref reg 90(2) (src:1416)
GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
      `hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate` hours `hourly rate` MEANS
    (hours TIMES `hourly rate` TIMES 52) DIVIDED BY 12

-- Paragraph (2): the individual threshold is the amount that a person of the same age as the claimant would be paid at the hourly rate
-- applicable under regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs; the rate is a stated
-- input) for (a) 16 hours a week, where the claimant would otherwise fall within section 20 or 21, or (b) the expected number of hours
-- per week (regulation 88), where the claimant would otherwise fall within section 22. A claimant who would otherwise fall within
-- section 19 has no individual threshold: the rule returns NOTHING.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- src:1413 | (2) A claimant's individual threshold is the amount that a person of the same age as the claimant would be paid at the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for—
-- src:1414 | (a) 16 hours per week, in the case of a claimant who would otherwise fall within section 20 (claimants subject to work-focused interview requirement only) or section 21 (claimants subject to work-preparation requirement) of the Act; or
-- src:1415 | (b) the expected number of hours per week in the case of a claimant who would otherwise fall within section 22 of the Act (claimants subject to all work-related requirements),
-- src:1416 | converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
@ref reg 90(2) (src:1413-1416)
GIVEN group IS A `Work-related group`
      `the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations to a person of the same age as the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 90(2) — the individual threshold` group `the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations to a person of the same age as the claimant` `the expected number of hours per week` MEANS
    CONSIDER group
    WHEN `subject to work-focused interview requirement only` THEN JUST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` 16 `the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations to a person of the same age as the claimant`)
    WHEN `subject to work-preparation requirement` THEN JUST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` 16 `the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations to a person of the same age as the claimant`)
    WHEN `subject to all work-related requirements` THEN JUST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` `the expected number of hours per week` `the hourly rate applicable under regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations to a person of the same age as the claimant`)
    WHEN `subject to no work-related requirements` THEN NOTHING

-- Paragraph (1): a claimant falls within section 19 if their monthly earnings are equal to or exceed their individual threshold.
-- src:1411 | 90 Claimants subject to no work-related requirements - the earnings thresholds
-- src:1412 | (1) A claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimants subject to no work-related requirements) if the claimant's monthly earnings are equal to or exceed the claimant's individual threshold.
@ref reg 90(1) (src:1411-1412)
GIVEN `monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `individual threshold` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 90(1) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the individual threshold` `monthly earnings` `individual threshold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `individual threshold`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST threshold THEN JUST (`monthly earnings` AT LEAST threshold)

-- Paragraph (3): a claimant who is a member of a couple falls within section 19 if the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed
-- (a) for joint claimants, the sum of their individual thresholds, or (b) for a claimant who claims as a single person by virtue of
-- regulation 3(3), the sum of the claimant's individual threshold and the amount paid for 35 hours a week at the hourly rate specified in
-- regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations. A single claimant who is not a member of a couple has no couple's threshold.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- src:1417 | (3) A claimant who is a member of a couple falls within section 19 of the Act if the couple's combined monthly earnings are equal to or exceed whichever of the following amounts is applicable—
-- src:1418 | (a) in the case of joint claimants, the sum of their individual thresholds; or
-- src:1419 | (b) in the case of a claimant who claims universal credit as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(3), the sum of—
-- src:1420 | (i) the claimant's individual threshold, and
-- src:1421 | (ii) the amount a person would be paid for 35 hours per week at the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations , converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
@ref reg 90(3) (src:1417-1421)
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
      `individual threshold of the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `individual threshold of the other joint claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 90(3) — the threshold for the couple's combined monthly earnings` basis `individual threshold of the claimant` `individual threshold of the other joint claimant` `the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a single claimant` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `joint claimants` THEN JUST (`individual threshold of the claimant` PLUS `individual threshold of the other joint claimant`)
    WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` THEN JUST (`individual threshold of the claimant` PLUS (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` 35 `the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`))

@ref reg 90(3) (src:1417-1421)
GIVEN `the couple's combined monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      threshold IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 90(3) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the threshold` `the couple's combined monthly earnings` threshold MEANS
    CONSIDER threshold
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (`the couple's combined monthly earnings` AT LEAST amount)

-- Paragraph (4): a claimant employed under a contract of apprenticeship falls within section 19 if their monthly earnings equal or exceed
-- the amount paid for (a) 30 hours a week or (b) if less, the expected number of hours per week, at the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d)
-- of the National Minimum Wage Regulations.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- src:1422 | (4) A claimant falls within section 19 of the Act if the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship and has monthly earnings that are equal to or exceed the amount they would be paid for—
-- src:1423 | (a) 30 hours a week; or
-- src:1424 | (b) if less, the expected number of hours per week for that claimant,
-- src:1425 | at the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations , converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
@ref reg 90(4) (src:1422-1425)
GIVEN `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 90(4) — the apprentice's monthly earnings equal or exceed the threshold` `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `monthly earnings` `the expected number of hours per week` `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship`
    AND (`monthly earnings` AT LEAST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` (minimum (LIST 30, `the expected number of hours per week`)) `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`))

-- Paragraph (5): a claimant falls within section 19 if treated as having earned income under regulation 62 (minimum income floor, uc2).
-- out of range: regulation 62 (piece uc2): whether the claimant is treated as having earned income is a stated input
-- src:1426 | (5) A claimant falls within section 19 of the Act if they are treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 (minimum income floor).
@ref reg 90(5) (src:1426)
GIVEN `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 90(5) — the claimant is treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor` `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62` MEANS
    `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62`

-- Paragraph (6): monthly earnings. (a) the person's earned income, calculated or estimated for the current assessment period before any
-- deduction for income tax, national insurance contributions or relievable pension contributions; or (b) where the earned income fluctuates
-- (or is likely to), that income taken as a monthly average over (i) one cycle if there is an identifiable cycle, or (ii) three months or
-- such other period as enables the average to be determined more accurately. The Secretary of State may disregard income from an
-- employment that has ceased: the averages are stated after any such disregard. Earned income is Part 6 (uc2): a stated input.
-- The comparison with a threshold that regulation 6(1A) has made a whole number of pounds gives the same answer whether or not the
-- earnings are rounded down, so the earnings are not rounded.
-- src:1427 | (6) A person’s monthly earnings are—
-- src:1428 | (a) the person’s earned income calculated or estimated in relation to the current assessment period before any deduction for income tax, national insurance contributions or relievable pension contributions; or
-- src:1429 | (b) in a case where the person's earned income fluctuates (or is likely to fluctuate) the amount of that income , calculated or estimated before any deduction for income tax, national insurance contributions or relievable pension contributions, taken as a monthly average—
-- src:1430 | (i) where there is an identifiable cycle, over the duration of one such cycle, or
-- src:1431 | (ii) where there is no identifiable cycle, over three months or such other period as may, in the particular case, enable the monthly average to be determined more accurately
-- src:1432 | and the Secretary of State may, in order to enable monthly earnings to be determined more accurately, disregard earned income received in respect of an employment which has ceased.
@ref reg 90(6) (src:1427-1432)
DECLARE `Earnings for the monthly earnings of regulation 90(6)` HAS
    `earned income calculated or estimated in relation to the current assessment period before any deduction`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the person's earned income fluctuates (or is likely to fluctuate)`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an identifiable cycle`                                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `monthly average over the duration of one such cycle`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `monthly average over three months or such other period as may enable the monthly average to be determined more accurately`   IS A NUMBER

@ref reg 90(6) (src:1427-1432)
GIVEN earnings IS AN `Earnings for the monthly earnings of regulation 90(6)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 90(6) — the person's monthly earnings` earnings MEANS
    IF earnings's `the person's earned income fluctuates (or is likely to fluctuate)`
    THEN (IF earnings's `there is an identifiable cycle`
          THEN earnings's `monthly average over the duration of one such cycle`
          ELSE earnings's `monthly average over three months or such other period as may enable the monthly average to be determined more accurately`)
    ELSE earnings's `earned income calculated or estimated in relation to the current assessment period before any deduction`

-- Paragraph (7) is a run of dots.
-- src:1433 | (7) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref reg 90(7) (src:1433)
`reg 90(7) — a run of dots in the text, not encoded` MEANS "(7) . . . ."

-- Regulation 90 as a whole: a claimant falls within section 19 if paragraph (1), (3), (4) or (5) applies. A route that returns NOTHING
-- (paragraph (1) for a claimant who has no individual threshold, paragraph (3) for a single claimant who is not a member of a couple)
-- is a route that does not apply, not a finding about the claimant.
@ref reg 90(1), (3), (4), (5) (src:1411-1426)
GIVEN `by paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 90 — the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by the earnings thresholds` `by paragraph (1)` `by paragraph (3)` `by paragraph (4)` `by paragraph (5)` MEANS
    `by paragraph (1) applies`
    OR `by paragraph (3) applies`
    OR `by paragraph (4)`
    OR `by paragraph (5)`
    WHERE
        `by paragraph (1) applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `by paragraph (1)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST result THEN result
        `by paragraph (3) applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `by paragraph (3)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST result THEN result

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 91 — Claimants subject to work-focused interview requirement only`

-- src:1434 | 91 Claimants subject to work-focused interview requirement only
-- src:1435 | (1) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref reg 91(1) (src:1434-1435)
`reg 91(1) — a run of dots in the text, not encoded` MEANS "(1) . . . ."

-- Paragraph (3): a "friend or family carer" is a person who is responsible for a child but is not the child's parent or step-parent, and
-- who has undertaken the care of the child because (a) the child has no parent or has parents unable to care, or (b) it is likely that the
-- child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns about the child's welfare.
-- out of range: regulation 4 (piece uc1): whether the claimant is responsible for the child is a stated input
-- out of range: regulation 5 (piece uc1): whether a person is a qualifying young person is a stated input
-- src:1442 | (3) In paragraph (2)(e) “friend or family carer” means a person who is responsible for a child, but is not the child's parent or step-parent, and has undertaken the care of the child in the following circumstances—
-- src:1443 | (a) the child has no parent or has parents who are unable to care for the child; or
-- src:1444 | (b) it is likely that the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns in relation to the child's welfare.
@ref reg 91(3) (src:1442-1444)
DECLARE `Friend or family carer facts` HAS
    `the claimant is responsible for the child`                                                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's relationship to the child`                                                                                                            IS A `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person`
    `the child has no parent or has parents who are unable to care for the child`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely that the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns in relation to the child's welfare`            IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 91(3) (src:1442-1444)
GIVEN carer IS A `Friend or family carer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(3) — friend or family carer` carer MEANS
    (carer's `the claimant is responsible for the child`)
    AND (NOT ((carer's `the claimant's relationship to the child`)'s `person is a parent of A`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 2 — step-parent` (carer's `the claimant's relationship to the child`)))
    AND (`no parent able to care` OR `otherwise looked after`)
    WHERE
        `no parent able to care` MEANS carer's `the child has no parent or has parents who are unable to care for the child`
        `otherwise looked after` MEANS carer's `it is likely that the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns in relation to the child's welfare`

-- Paragraph (2), limbs (a) to (c): foster parents. (a) the responsible foster parent in relation to a child aged at least 1; (b) the
-- responsible foster parent in relation to a qualifying young person, where the Secretary of State is satisfied that the qualifying young
-- person has care needs making it unreasonable to require a work search or work availability requirement; (c) a foster parent, but not the
-- responsible foster parent, in relation to a child or qualifying young person, on the same satisfaction.
-- out of range: regulation 5 (piece uc1): whether a person is a qualifying young person is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1436 | (2) A claimant falls within section 20 of the Act if—
-- src:1437 | (a) the claimant is the responsible foster parent in relation to a child aged at least 1;
-- src:1438 | (b) the claimant is the responsible foster parent in relation to a qualifying young person, and the Secretary of State is satisfied that the qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act;
-- src:1439 | (c) the claimant is a foster parent, but not the responsible foster parent, in relation to a child or qualifying young person, and the Secretary of State is satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act;
@ref reg 91(2)(a) to (c) (src:1436-1439)
DECLARE `Fostered person facts` HAS
    `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person`                                                                                                                                                                                       IS A `Foster parents of a child`
    `the person fostered is a child`                                                                                                                                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person fostered is a qualifying young person`                                                                                                                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person fostered is aged at least 1`                                                                                                                                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 91(2)(a) (src:1436-1439)
GIVEN fostered IS A `Fostered person facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2)(a) — the responsible foster parent of a child aged at least 1` fostered MEANS
    (`reg 85 — responsible foster parent` (fostered's `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person`))
    AND (fostered's `the person fostered is a child`)
    AND (fostered's `the person fostered is aged at least 1`)

@ref reg 91(2)(b) (src:1436-1439)
GIVEN fostered IS A `Fostered person facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2)(b) — the responsible foster parent of a qualifying young person with care needs` fostered MEANS
    (`reg 85 — responsible foster parent` (fostered's `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person`))
    AND (fostered's `the person fostered is a qualifying young person`)
    AND (fostered's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act`)

@ref reg 91(2)(c) (src:1436-1439)
GIVEN fostered IS A `Fostered person facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2)(c) — a foster parent who is not the responsible foster parent, with care needs` fostered MEANS
    (`reg 2 — foster parent` ((fostered's `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person`)'s `the claimant's placement of the child`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 85 — responsible foster parent` (fostered's `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person`)))
    AND ((fostered's `the person fostered is a child`) OR (fostered's `the person fostered is a qualifying young person`))
    AND (fostered's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act`)

-- Limb (d): the claimant has fallen within limb (a), (b) or (c) within the past 8 weeks, has no child or qualifying young person currently
-- placed with them, but expects to resume being a foster parent.
-- out of range: regulation 5 (piece uc1): whether a person is a qualifying young person is a stated input
-- src:1440 | (d) the claimant has fallen within sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c) within the past 8 weeks and has no child or qualifying young person currently placed with them, but expects to resume being a foster parent; or
@ref reg 91(2)(d) (src:1440)
GIVEN `date on which the claimant last fell within sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant has no child or qualifying young person currently placed with them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant expects to resume being a foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2)(d) — a foster parent between placements` `date on which the claimant last fell within sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` `the claimant has no child or qualifying young person currently placed with them` `the claimant expects to resume being a foster parent` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `within the past 8 weeks`
    AND `the claimant has no child or qualifying young person currently placed with them`
    AND `the claimant expects to resume being a foster parent`
    WHERE
        `within the past 8 weeks` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date on which the claimant last fell within sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST last THEN
                ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day last) AT LEAST 0)
                AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day last) AT MOST 56)

-- Limb (e): the claimant has become a friend or family carer in relation to a child within the past 12 months and is also the responsible
-- carer in relation to that child.
-- src:1441 | (e) the claimant has become a friend or family carer in relation to a child within the past 12 months and is also the responsible carer in relation to that child.
@ref reg 91(2)(e) (src:1441)
GIVEN carer IS A `Friend or family carer facts`
      `date on which the claimant became a friend or family carer` IS A DATE
      `the claimant is also the responsible carer in relation to that child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2)(e) — a friend or family carer within 12 months` carer `date on which the claimant became a friend or family carer` `the claimant is also the responsible carer in relation to that child` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    (`reg 91(3) — friend or family carer` carer)
    AND `within the past 12 months`
    AND `the claimant is also the responsible carer in relation to that child`
    WHERE
        `within the past 12 months` MEANS
            ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date on which the claimant became a friend or family carer`) AT LEAST 0)
            AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `date on which the claimant became a friend or family carer` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))) AT MOST 0)

-- Paragraph (2): a claimant falls within section 20 of the Act if any of limbs (a) to (e) applies.
@ref reg 91(2) (src:1436-1441)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 91(2) — the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` a b c d e MEANS
    any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb) (LIST a, b, c, d, e)

