§§ `Regulations 91A and 92 — omitted`

-- The line of dots under each heading cannot be quoted: srcrefs reads a run of dots as an ellipsis, and a quotation of nothing but
-- an ellipsis has no text. The coverage table row for each says what the text shows.
-- src:1445 | 91A Claimants subject to work preparation requirement
@ref reg 91A (src:1445)
`reg 91A — a run of dots in the text under the heading "Claimants subject to work preparation requirement", not encoded` MEANS "91A . . . ."

-- src:1447 | 92 Claimants subject to all work-related requirements - EEA jobseekers
@ref reg 92 (src:1447)
`reg 92 — a run of dots in the text under the heading "Claimants subject to all work-related requirements - EEA jobseekers", not encoded` MEANS "92 . . . ."
